DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T170000
UID:6a85f7f3be14820029888297@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover the exciting world of coding with the Dash Robot!\nIn
  this hands-on program\, children will learn the basics of programming by 
 using simple\, block-based coding to make Dash move\, dance\, light up\, p
 lay sounds\, and navigate obstacles. Through fun challenges\, games\, and 
 creative activities\, participants will build problem-solving\, critical t
 hinking\, and teamwork skills while exploring STEM concepts in an engaging
  and interactive way.\nNo previous coding experience is required. Recommen
 ded for children ages 6–12.
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Auditorium\, Lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85f7f3be14820029888297
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
