SUMMARY:Artists in the Library:  Woodland Strawberry Felt Collage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T160000
UID:6a84ba3869166f088b931e84@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 1 of a series of workshops for children and adults\, expl
 oring local flora through embroidery and felt collage. Hosted by Artist in
  the Library\, Sarah Zenchetta.\nAll ages\nprogram\; children ages 6 to 14
  must be accompanied by a parent or caregiver.  Registration is required. 
 Space is limited.\nNote:\nEach workshop requires separate registration. Re
 gistered participant spaces are held for 15 minutes after which drop-ins a
 re allowed\nMeet the Resident:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) is a queer text
 ile artist and educator whose practice dives into the loss of connection a
 nd knowledge of poisonous plants in North America. Zanchetta uses textiles
 \, texts\, and hosts community workshops to create intimate works and spac
 es where we can unfold our curiosities\, care and anxieties about what gro
 ws beside our feet. She holds a Master of Visual Studies from the Univers
 ity of Toronto (2023) and a BFA from OCAD University (2018).\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84ba3869166f088b931e84
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
