BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Camp Canva
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T170000
UID:6a4e5d67717ad787031571f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this three-part Canva class for beginners\, learners will d
 esign posters\, edit videos\, and create a slideshow.\nBasic mouse and key
 board skills required.\nFriday\, August 14\nWeek 1: Poster Design\nLearn
  how to artfully arrange basic poster elements using Canva.\nFriday\,\nAug
 ust 21\nWeek 2: Animation Basics\nLearn how to make a basic short video wi
 th transitions\, text\, and music using Canva.\nFriday\,\nAugust 28\nWeek 
 3: Slideshow Skills\nLearn how to make a basic slideshow presentation usin
 g Canva.\nRegistration for all three classes is required.\nRegistration fo
 r this program opens one month before the program date.\nFor ages 6 - 12 o
 nly.\nFor all registered Children's programs at Malvern\, there is a grace
  period of 10 minutes. After the first 10 minutes of a program\, spots wil
 l be given to waiting customers.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4e5d67717ad787031571f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
