BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orange Shirt Day Storytime and Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T150000
UID:6a84a28fbe14820029882c95@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special reading of Phyllis’s Orange Shirt by P
 hyllis Webstad and When We Are Kind by Monique Gray Smith in honour of Ora
 nge Shirt Day. After the storytime\, kids can get creative by making heart
  crafts and decorating their own paper orange shirt to celebrate kindness\
 , caring and friendship\, and honour the truth that Every Child Matters.\n
 Ages: 12 & under.\nDrop–in only.  No registration required.\nThis is a s
 taff-led program that uses materials developed by The Orange Shirt Society
 .
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84a28fbe14820029882c95
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
