BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adobe Design Camp: Photo\, Illustration and Video Editing (August 
 24th-27th)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260824T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T110000
UID:6a5fd055f4e5db3d00c34c30@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all future animators\, graphic artists\, and video edi
 tors!\nReady to learn the industry-standard tools used by professional des
 igners and creators around the world? Join us for an action-packed\, 4-day
  creative boot camp where you’ll turn your imagination into digital mast
 erpieces.\nFrom custom digital illustrations to live-animated characters a
 nd slick video edits\, this hands-on workshop gives you the ultimate creat
 ive toolkit!\nWhat We’re Learning:\nDay 1: Adobe Photoshop\n– Master d
 igital photo editing\, photo manipulation\, and graphic creation secrets.\
 nDay 2: Adobe Character Animator\n– Bring your drawings to life! Learn h
 ow to animate characters using your own motion and voice in real time.\nDa
 y 3: Adobe Illustrator\n– Dive into vector design to build create a mons
 ter/character using the shape builder tool and others.\nDay 4: Adobe Premi
 ere Pro\n– Put it all together! Slice clips\, add sound\, and polish vid
 eo edits into a smooth final production.\nThe Details:\nWho:\nCreative kid
 s ages\n8 to 12\nWhen:\nMonday through Thursday\,\n10:00 AM – 11:00 AM\n
 Where:\n[Agincourt Library/Learning Centre]\n⚠️\nImportant Note:\nThis
  is a sequential\, cumulative program. Because each day builds directly on
  the last\,\nregistrants must attend all 4 sessions\nto participate.\nSpac
 e is limited\, and spots fill up fast. Grab your spot starting on August 1
 0th at 9 a.m.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5fd055f4e5db3d00c34c30
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
